From 2f1f01b109a02f1098207239bd5b0933cc12c116 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:34:06 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Pull in the libcamera userspace for the IPU6 cameras

The cameras of the IPU6 based Surface devices (Surface Pro 8, Pro 9)
are raw sensors: applications can only use them through libcamera and
its software ISP, normally via the PipeWire camera portal. Pull in the
PipeWire libcamera plugin and the libcamera IPA modules (which contain
the software ISP control algorithms) as weak dependencies, so that the
cameras work out of the box.
---
 redhat/kernel.spec.template | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/redhat/kernel.spec.template b/redhat/kernel.spec.template
index b371a121..9053d9cd 100644
--- a/redhat/kernel.spec.template
+++ b/redhat/kernel.spec.template
@@ -1254,6 +1254,8 @@ Requires(pre): %{initrd_prereq}\
 Requires(pre): ((linux-firmware >= 20150904-56.git6ebf5d57) if linux-firmware)\
 Recommends: linux-firmware\
 Recommends: intel-vsc-firmware\
+Recommends: libcamera-ipa\
+Recommends: pipewire-plugin-libcamera\
 Recommends: iptsd\
 Recommends: %{package_name}-default-watchdog\
 Requires(preun): systemd >= 200\
-- 
